title: $:/nikorion/language/en-GB/ThemeNotice/

Title: ! Everything you edit or create here becomes the theme
Rule: ''In this dev wiki, whatever you create or modify from the web interface is part of the theme.'' It is written into the plugin sources and removed from `wiki/tiddlers/`: you build the theme directly in the browser.
Why: The dev server watches what the browser saves. A tiddler the theme already ships updates its source file: Vanilla's stylesheets and settings in `src/pkm-theme/vanilla/`, the author's stylesheets in `styles/`, overrides of core and third-party tiddlers in `overrides/`. A new one is created there too: a stylesheet in `styles/`, an image in `images/`, anything else in `overrides/`. Edits to the Nikorion palette (`$:/palettes/nikorion`) go to the TW-PKM-Palette plugin. Only works while `pnpm dev` runs.
Where: Never taken: drafts, session state, and the tiddlers that were already files of this wiki when the server started (this one, Playground, site title, `$:/layout`…): their edits stay in the wiki. The layout is not part of the theme: `layout` keeps providing it. Check `git status` in TW-PKM-Theme (and TW-PKM-Palette) after a session.
Manual: ''Creating a file by hand in `wiki/tiddlers/` while `pnpm dev` runs would make the plugin swallow it as theme.'' Create wiki content (a demo, a note) before starting `pnpm dev`, or stop the server while you do it.
